WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.239 --> 00:00:15.380
bragged to the other boys: "Aha!

2
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.060
I have shot the Wendy Bird.

3
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.881
Peter will be so proud of me."

4
00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:25.242
"This is no bird," said Slightly.

5
00:00:25.262 --> 00:00:26.903
"It's a girl!"

6
00:00:26.923 --> 00:00:31.644
"Now I understand," said Curly.

7
00:00:32.812 --> 00:00:35.653
"Maybe Peter was bringing her here to take care of us."

8
00:00:35.673 --> 00:00:38.954
"And you have killed her!"

9
00:00:39.654 --> 00:00:40.474
scolded Nibs.

10
00:00:41.755 --> 00:00:44.915
Tootle's face turned white when he realized his mistake.

11
00:00:46.516 --> 00:00:50.017
He was now afraid of what Peter would say and of how he would be punished.

12
00:00:51.857 --> 00:00:53.638
It was a very tragic moment.

13
00:00:54.918 --> 00:00:57.699
All the boys looked down in deep regret and sorrow.

14
00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:01.620
Just then, they heard a crowing from up above.

15
00:01:02.932 --> 00:01:05.253
This was Peter's usual signal to the boys.

16
00:01:05.273 --> 00:01:07.535
"It's Peter!"

17
00:01:08.255 --> 00:01:09.136
the boys cried.

18
00:01:09.156 --> 00:01:13.198
"We must hide her," whispered Nibs.

19
00:01:14.539 --> 00:01:18.041
Nodding, the others crowded around Wendy's body in confusion.

20
00:01:18.061 --> 00:01:23.764
"Greetings, boys," said Peter as he dropped down from the sky.

21
00:01:23.784 --> 00:01:25.885
"I have good news.

22
00:01:26.305 --> 00:01:28.726
I've brought a mother to take care of us all."

23
00:01:29.947 --> 00:01:31.128
He looked around at his boys.

24
00:01:32.156 --> 00:01:34.418
There were none of the usual salutes or cheers.

25
00:01:34.438 --> 00:01:37.340
"Why aren't you cheering me?"

26
00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:38.260
he asked.

27
00:01:38.881 --> 00:01:40.101
"Why so sad?"

28
00:01:42.463 --> 00:01:45.945
The boys stepped aside for Peter to see and then pointed to the body.

29
00:01:48.087 --> 00:01:52.830
"She's dead," said Peter, as he pulled the arrow from Wendy's chest.

30
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.991
"Who did this?"

31
00:01:57.933 --> 00:02:01.656
When Tootles admitted his mistake, Peter raised his arm to hit him.

32
00:02:02.656 --> 00:02:04.256
But a small hand stopped him.

33
00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:07.217
Wendy wasn't quite dead yet.

34
00:02:08.418 --> 00:02:11.338
Even in her weak state, she had protected Tootles.

35
00:02:11.358 --> 00:02:14.179
"She lives!"

36
00:02:14.819 --> 00:02:16.260
the boys shouted with joy.

37
00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:21.141
Peter knelt beside her and found the acorn button he had given her.

38
00:02:22.381 --> 00:02:24.242
It was still on a chain around her neck.

39
00:02:25.442 --> 00:02:27.503
It had protected her from the arrow.

40
00:02:27.523 --> 00:02:32.084
"That's the kiss I gave her, and it has saved her life.

41
00:02:33.396 --> 00:02:34.978
I'm such a hero!"

42
00:02:35.618 --> 00:02:36.259
cried Peter.

43
00:02:36.279 --> 00:02:42.183
"Hooray!" Now the boys had something to cheer about.

44
00:02:43.324 --> 00:02:44.865
Only Tinker Bell was miserable.

45
00:02:45.986 --> 00:02:48.068
The boys told Peter what she had said to them.

46
00:02:49.429 --> 00:02:51.331
"Tink, I'm ashamed of you!"

47
00:02:52.031 --> 00:02:52.652
said Peter.

48
00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.753
"Out of my sight!

49
00:02:55.054 --> 00:02:56.675
I don't want to see you anymore."

50
00:02:57.996 --> 00:03:00.618
Tinker Bell flew down and landed on Peter's arm.

51
00:03:01.839 --> 00:03:02.880
She pleaded with him.

52
00:03:04.012 --> 00:03:07.975
But Wendy, still lying as if dead, raised her arm again.

53
00:03:09.116 --> 00:03:12.098
Feeling a bit sorry for the fairy, Peter gave in.

54
00:03:12.118 --> 00:03:16.541
"Well, maybe I won't banish you forever.

55
00:03:17.421 --> 00:03:19.183
But at least for a whole week!"

56
00:03:20.684 --> 00:03:24.146
Even so, Tinker Bell was not the least bit grateful to Wendy.

57
00:03:25.247 --> 00:03:28.149
In fact, she wanted to pinch Wendy even more.

58
00:03:28.169 --> 00:03:32.732
"Let's carry Wendy down to the house," Curly suggested.

59
00:03:33.848 --> 00:03:36.689
"But we shouldn't touch her," said Tootles.

60
00:03:37.829 --> 00:03:40.950
"We might accidentally hurt her even more."

61
00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:46.812
"If she lies here in the open overnight, she'll die," argued Slightly.

62
00:03:46.832 --> 00:03:53.474
"Well then, let's build a temporary little house around her right here," suggested Peter.

63
00:03:53.494 --> 00:03:56.614
"Bring me the best of what each of you have.

64
00:03:57.535 --> 00:04:01.856
You can take it from our house," he ordered in his captain's voice.

65
00:04:03.149 --> 00:04:10.595
Happy to follow Peter's orders again, the boys went about finding soft bedding, firewood, and anything else they

66
00:04:10.635 --> 00:04:11.195
could think of.

67
00:04:12.096 --> 00:04:16.700
They went up and down and all around, working hard to make their new mother comfortable.

68
00:04:18.061 --> 00:04:20.763
Suddenly, John and Michael appeared in the sky.

69
00:04:22.164 --> 00:04:24.386
They too were relieved to see Peter again.

70
00:04:24.406 --> 00:04:27.068
"Hello, Peter!"

71
00:04:27.709 --> 00:04:28.269
they yelled.

72
00:04:28.289 --> 00:04:31.572
"Hello," Peter replied.

73
00:04:32.512 --> 00:04:34.433
He had actually forgotten all about them.

74
00:04:35.614 --> 00:04:39.656
Peter was busy measuring Wendy to see how large the new house would need to be.

75
00:04:41.137 --> 00:04:44.238
John and Michael watched the frantic activity around them.

76
00:04:44.258 --> 00:04:46.860
"Is Wendy asleep?"

77
00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:50.322
asked John, seeing his sister on the ground.

78
00:04:50.342 --> 00:04:53.603
"Let's wake her up," said Michael.

79
00:04:53.623 --> 00:04:55.705
"She can make our dinner."

80
00:04:55.725 --> 00:04:58.266
"Yes, we're hungry!"

81
00:04:58.926 --> 00:04:59.667
John shouted.

82
00:04:59.687 --> 00:05:02.920
"Maybe later," said Peter.

83
00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:07.843
"Now you can help the others carry branches to build a house for your sister."

84
00:05:07.863 --> 00:05:10.325
"A house for Wendy?"

85
00:05:10.885 --> 00:05:11.825
John exclaimed.

86
00:05:11.845 --> 00:05:13.747
"She's only a girl."

87
00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:16.588
"But she's going to be our mother.

88
00:05:17.048 --> 00:05:20.490
We must be respectful and kind," explained Curly.
